    "ss_vs_external_scan_discrepancy": {
      "observation": "Reproduced identically to the 2026-09-10 run: at the 'restored' phase, `ss -ltn` shows port 6379 (native, non-Docker Redis) bound to 0.0.0.0, but the off-host container scan does not report it reachable, while every Docker-published port (5432/6380/8080/8096/9000) is both bound and reachable despite ufw being active with a default-deny-incoming policy allowing only port 22.",
      "root_cause": "Same as 2026-09-10: ufw filters the host's own INPUT chain (catching the native redis-server on 6379), but Docker's own iptables DNAT/FORWARD rules for published ports take effect ahead of ufw's filter chain and are unaffected by it -- exactly the mechanism hostveil's `firewall.docker-bypass` finding (internal/check/firewall) describes. Not re-verified with fresh `ufw status`/`docker ps` output on this specific VM instance since it reproduced the identical port pattern; the mechanism was already confirmed with direct evidence on 2026-09-10."
    }
  },
