      "not_investigated_further": "Not root-caused in this session -- this is a NEW discrepancy, different in direction from the one traced in experiment A/B (there, ss showed something scan didn't; here external reachability shrank while ss stayed flat). Candidate explanations not yet tested: transient flakiness in the extscan container's own connect-timing heuristic (scripts/measure/instruments/extscan.sh notes busybox `nc -w` only bounds connect time, not read time), or a docker bridge/NAT re-initialization triggered by restart_services()'s `docker compose up -d` calls even though no container was recreated. Reported as an honest, unresolved fact rather than smoothed over or explained away without evidence -- consistent with this session's prior finding that ss and the external scan can legitimately disagree, but this specific direction of disagreement has not been traced to a mechanism the way the docker-bypass case was."
